<title>USA: Analysts' estimates for U.S. cotton plantings.</title>
<headline>Analysts' estimates for U.S. cotton plantings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are analysts' estimates for U.S. plantings (in million acres). USDA is to release its estimates Monday at 0830 EST/1330 GMT.</p>
<p>    Average:   14.0075</p>
<p>    Range:     13.7-14.25</p>
<p>    USDA 1996: 14.67</p>
<p>Carl Anderson, Texas A &amp; M University -- 13.7</p>
<p>David Brandon, Smith Barney -- 14.2</p>
<p>O.A. Cleveland, Mississippi State University -- 13.9</p>
<p>Judith Ganes, Merrill Lynch -- 14.065</p>
<p>Sharon Johnson, Frank Schneider and Co Inc -- 13.9</p>
<p>Jarral Neeper, Calcot Ltd -- 14.25</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
